.TH FZFM 1 "March 2025" "fzfm" "File Managers"
.SH NAME
fzfm \- Fuzzy File Manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fzfm
.SH DESCRIPTION
fzfm is a terminal-based file manager using fzf for fuzzy finding.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B Enter
Open file or directory
.TP
.B Left
Go to parent directory
.TP
.B Right
Open file or directory
.TP
.B Space
Toggle selection (multi-select)
.TP
.B alt\-c
Copy selected files to clipboard
.TP
.B alt\-m
Move selected files to clipboard
.TP
.B alt\-p
Paste copied/moved files to current directory
.TP
.B alt\-r
Rename selected file
.TP
.B alt\-d
Create new directory
.TP
.B alt\-f
Create new file
.TP
.B alt\-t
Move selected files to trash
.TP
.B alt\-up / alt\-down
Navigate preview window
.TP
.B alt\-s
Play video in fullscreen (mpv)
.TP
.B alt\-b
Set image as wallpaper
.TP
.B F1
Show help
.TP
.B Esc
Clear clipboard and exit
.SH CONFIGURATION
fzfm requires the following commands:
.BR lsd (1), fzf (1)
.PP
Optional for image previews:
.BR chafa (1), viu (1), kitten (1)
.PP
Optional for video previews:
.BR ffmpeg (1), ffprobe (1)
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/copied
Temporary storage for copied/moved files
.TP
.I /tmp/fzf_video_cache
Thumbnail cache for video previews
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fzf (1), lsd (1), bat (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jake@Linux
